{
  "_about": "Curated free-text compound-meal scenarios for the recipe-decomposer lab (_smoke_decomposer_lab.py). Each runs the FULL decompose() pipeline (catalog preference + reconstruction-gated override + compound-meal gate all active) and is checked on: compound-gate detection, survival of must_keep components, plausible per-100 g energy density, the path that fired vs expected, and that no dish was collapsed onto a SINGLE-ingredient catalog food. Bands are generous — the lab flags outliers for human review, it is not a brittle CI gate. compound = the EXPECTED output of _is_compound_meal (documents the gate's actual reach, incl. its comma-list limitation). must_keep[*].any_of = a component survives if ANY synonym matches an ingredient's description or food group.",
